      "message": "Looking at the Rust docs for OsString/CString probably not an issue, just something to keep in mind - we should be extra careful that the APKs are interpreted the same way as Android does. From libziparchive, that means decoding paths as UTF-8 with no zero bytes. That is what OsString does. But converting to and comparing as CString should be safe as long as that UTF-8 really has no zero bytes.",
