      "message": "I missed this comment. Yes, we need to be careful. If my understanding is correct, OsString does allow zero bytes in the middle (just like String does), while CString doesn\u0027t. So conversion from OsString to CString can fail (the return type of CString::new is Result) or at least lossy. But if libziparchive doesn\u0027t allow zero bytes in the middle, we are doing the same by using CString.",
